    turnFlow: 'The player with the highest double sets it as the spinner. Going clockwise, each player must play a tile matching the spinner until four tiles are around it (phase one). A player unable to play draws one tile from the boneyard; if it can play they set it, otherwise they keep it and pass. Once four arms are started, each player must add a double to the end of any arm (crosswise); all four arms must be completed (phase two). After that, doubles are played crosswise and non-doubles in line from the ends of the arms. Play continues until one player dominoes or the game blocks.',
